# The GPUI client's desktop entry, for packaging (a later task; see README.md here). Not installed by
# anything in this repository, and never registered on a development machine: the installed Electron
# client owns `decibell://` there.
#
# - The file's name is the desktop id the app uses everywhere: the window's Wayland `app_id` and X11
#   `WM_CLASS` are "decibell" (crates/decibell-app/src/window.rs), and the launcher progress names
#   `application://decibell.desktop` (crates/decibell-platform/src/progress.rs). Keep the three in step.
# - `%U`: the desktop passes a `decibell://invite/<code>` link as an argument; a running instance takes
#   it over (crates/decibell-platform/src/instance.rs). The package's install step registers the
#   handler with the system (`update-desktop-database`); the app itself never changes the default
#   (Electron re-pointed it at every start: HANDOFF.md §4, Electron findings).
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Decibell
GenericName=Chat
Comment=Text, voice and screen sharing with your communities
Exec=decibell %U
Icon=decibell
Terminal=false
Categories=Network;Chat;InstantMessaging;
MimeType=x-scheme-handler/decibell;
StartupWMClass=decibell
StartupNotify=true
